    "abstract": "<jats:title>Abstract</jats:title>\n               <jats:p>The results of 3611 intensified CCD observations of double stars, made with the 26 inch refractor of the U.S. Naval Observatory, are presented. Each observation of a system represents a combination of over 2000 short-exposure images. These observations are averaged into 1857 mean relative positions and range in separation from 0.\u2033341 to 128.\u2033644, with a median separation of 6.\u2033533. Two systems have their orbits improved and one has its first determination. This is the 24th in this series of papers and covers the period 2018 May 24 through 2019 October 28.</jats:p>",
